dialogue greenvalley_recruit_mage
title: A caster on the ridge
trigger: StageCleared greenvalley-01
speaker commander $commander
speaker recruit $recruit
speaker backer $party:2

node meet recruit
  Easy, I'm not with the Choir. I followed the smoke from Saltmoss. You're the ones who stole their white wagon?
  -> reply

node reply commander
  That depends on who's asking, and why there's fire in your hand.
  * We did. Want to help us keep it? -> bold
  * Who's asking? -> wary
  * Put the fire out first. -> hands

node bold recruit
  Help? I've wanted to set that wagon alight since I was old enough to spell "tithe". Keeping it is a new idea.
  -> purpose

node wary recruit
  Someone from the fens. Someone the tithe line has missed twice, and I don't plan to give it a third go.
  -> purpose

node hands recruit
  That's not a threat, it's a habit. Fen folk keep a spark lit the way you'd keep a hand on a purse. There. Out.
  -> purpose

node purpose recruit
  So what's a white wagon for, once it isn't the Choir's?
  -> answer

node answer commander
  It was full of the tithe when we took it.
  * Getting the tithe out of the Choir's hands. -> cause
  * It was the fastest thing in Saltmoss. -> honest

node cause recruit
  Good answer. Everyone on the moor gives that answer, right up until the Captain's riders crest the hill.
  -> doubt

node honest recruit
  Ha. At least you don't dress it up. The last people who stole from the Choir called it a holy war.
  -> doubt

node doubt recruit
  Three of you against the whole moor, and the Captain on your heels. Why would anyone throw in with that?
  -> backer

node backer backer
  Show them the orb, Commander. Out here an orb is a dead stone, but near you they wake. We saw it at Saltmoss.
  -> orb

node orb recruit
  That orb's been dead since before my grandmother was born. It's glowing. How is it glowing?
  -> ask

node ask commander
  The light steadies in the Commander's palm.
  * It wakes near me. I don't know why yet. -> truth
  * Ride with us and find out. -> offer
  * Riding with us won't be safe. -> warned

node truth recruit
  Nobody on this moor admits to not knowing things. The Choir knows everything, and look where that got us.
  -> aunt

node offer recruit
  You're bargaining with my curiosity. It's working, and I'm annoyed that it's working.
  -> aunt

node aunt recruit
  The tithe took my aunt. She walked out of the line white as chalk and never warmed again. If that orb can wake, maybe other things can too.
  -> joined

node warned recruit
  Safe is the tithe line. I watched my aunt walk out of one white as chalk. I'll take the moor.
  -> joined

node joined recruit
  Then I'm in. In the fens we know what the tithe really takes, and how to make it burn back.
  do: JoinHero redmage role=Mage
  * Glad to have you, Red Mage. -> welcome
    do: AddTrust $recruit 10
  * You can thank the one who spoke for you. -> credit
    do: AddTrust $recruit 5
    do: AddCohesion $recruit $party:2 10
  * Keep that fire pointed at the Choir, not at us. -> terms
    do: AddTrust $recruit -5
    do: AddCohesion $recruit $party:2 5

node welcome recruit
  Glad to be had. Don't make me regret it before supper.

node credit backer
  Someone had to. You'd have talked yourself out of it otherwise.
  -> thanks

node thanks recruit
  Then I owe you a spark when you need one. Fen folk pay their debts. It's the Choir we don't pay.

node terms recruit
  Fair. I'll aim. I can't promise where it lands when the Captain's riders come.
